==English==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|en|some|how}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsʌmhaʊ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-somehow.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊ|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In one [[way]] or [[another]]; in a way not yet known or explained; by some means
#: {{usex|en|This problem has to be tackled '''somehow'''.}}
#: {{usex|en|We don't know how he's still alive after the accident, but '''somehow''' he is.}}
#* '''December 1, 2016''', Tom Donaghy writing in ''The New York Times'', ''[https://www.nytimes.com/2016/12/01/theater/edward-albee-friends.htmlThe Tender Side of Edward Albee]''
#*: It’s not by accident Edward wrote “The Goat,” “The Zoo Story” or “Seascape,” with its two lizards, Sarah and Leslie. In fact, in all of his plays the animal is pretty prominent, '''somehow''' or other.
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=II|text=Carried '''somehow''', somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers, of errand not wholly obvious to their fellows, yet of such sort as to call into query alike the nature of their errand and their own relations.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1895|author=William Dean Howells|title=Mortality
|passage=Have I not loathed to live again and said<br>It would have been far better to be dead,<br> And yet '''somehow''', I know not why, <br>Remained afraid to die!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1817| author=Sir {{w|Walter Scott}}| title=[[w:Rob Roy (novel)|Rob Roy]]| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=mMmJVBt5QRoC| passage=Although youngest of the family, he has <u>'''somehow''' or other</u> got the entire management of all the others.}}

====Usage notes====
The indefiniteness of somehow is emphasized by the addition of ''or other'', ''or another'' or ''or the other''.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|somewise}}
* {{l|en|someway}}

====Derived terms====
{{der2|en|somehow or other}}

